      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should be very cautious about taking a large dose of potassium chloride right now. While dehydration and electrolyte imbalance are possible after intense exercise, taking a sudden, high amount of potassium can be dangerous for your heart. Instead, start by sipping on an electrolyte drink or a glass of coconut water to gently rehydrate and replenish minerals. If your symptoms persist, it is best to consult a healthcare professional immediately.",
