      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is important to understand that while supplements are generally safe, a sudden, massive dose of potassium can cause serious cardiac issues, not just fix cramps. A racing heart combined with severe cramping warrants more than just a supplement, as it could indicate something more serious than simple dehydration. For rapid relief, try a small, measured dose of a balanced electrolyte mix, or focus on a cool down and rest, and if your heart rate doesn't settle, seek medical attention.",
      "source": "target",
