      "content": "Even 1000mg of potassium chloride taken without professional guidance can still be too much and potentially affect your heart rhythm, so I strongly advise against self-treating this way. Dizziness and a racing heart after intense exercise are signals that should not be ignored, even if you think it's just exhaustion. Please try drinking a full glass of water with a pinch of salt and some citrus juice, and if you feel any palpitations or worsening dizziness, please call a nurse line for advice instead of the ER.",
      "source": "target",
